{"name":"Icebreaker","hex":"#b7c2cc","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"icebreaker","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A ship designed to break through ice so that it, or other ships coming behind, can navigate on frozen seas.","A game, activity, humorous anecdote, etc., designed to ease tension and encourage interaction among individuals in a situation where they do not know each other well."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/icebreaker"}],"entries":[{"title":"Icebreaker","blocks":[{"text":"An icebreaker is a special-purpose ship or boat designed to move and navigate through ice-covered waters, and provide safe waterways for other boats and ships. Although the term usually refers to ice-breaking ships, it may also refer to smaller vessels, such as the icebreaking boats that were once used on the canals of the United Kingdom."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/97/120106-G-IA651-272_%286668116881%29.jpg/330px-120106-G-IA651-272_%286668116881%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Icebreaker","wikidata":"Q14978"},{"title":"Icebreaker (band)","blocks":[{"text":"Icebreaker is a UK-based new music ensemble founded by James Poke and John Godfrey. They interpret new music, specialising in a post-minimal and \"totalist\" repertoire. Icebreaker always play amplified and have a reputation for playing, by classical standards, \"seriously loud\". They have expanded their repertoire to include non-classical material, particularly in their version of the Brian Eno album Apollo, a project based on the music of Kraftwerk, and music by Scott Walker."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6c/Icebreaker_live_at_QEH_2010.jpg/330px-Icebreaker_live_at_QEH_2010.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Icebreaker_(band)","wikidata":"Q5985590"}],